    "conclusion": "Sixteen is the age at which Algeria’s compulsory schooling ends and a family’s options widen, and the east is where those options have been thinnest. A Cambridge record built alongside school through the middle years, then either continued beside the lycée or taken full-time with the destination in view, gives a student in Constantine or Annaba the same choices as one in Algiers. Book an assessment and we will plan those years with you."
