    "intro": "Addis Ababa is one of the very few cities in the world that is a diplomatic capital for a whole continent. The African Union has its headquarters here, so does the UN Economic Commission for Africa, and the embassy and NGO community that follows them is large. Alongside them sits a second group that gets less attention: Ethiopian families who built careers in Washington, London, Toronto or Frankfurt and have come home to invest, often with children who have only ever studied in English. This guide is about both groups, what Addis already offers them, and where a live online school honestly fits.",
