        "p": "Addis has good international schools. ICS Addis, Sandford International School, the German International School and Bingham Academy are established and well known, and many diplomatic families are well served by them. The pressure points are places in popular year groups, the commute across a fast-growing city, and fit: a returnee child from Maryland may need the American curriculum with AP, while a sibling who started in London needs Cambridge. Many Ethiopian families choose a strong local private school instead, where Amharic, Ethiopian history and the national route are taught properly, and then look for a way to add an English-medium international qualification on top. Those families are not choosing between schools; they are choosing how to add one qualification without giving up another."
