        "p": "Ethiopia runs on East Africa Time, the same as our Nairobi teaching base, all year. The only translation is cultural: in the Ethiopian way of telling time, a 4pm class is ten o’clock in the day, and the Ethiopian calendar runs its own year. Neither affects the timetable. Demand here is specific. Diplomatic and NGO families want A Level Mathematics, Economics and the sciences that survive the next posting. Returnees bound for American universities want AP Calculus, AP Biology and AP English. Families thinking of medicine or engineering want Chemistry and Physics taught by specialists. Every lesson is recorded, which matters when power or connectivity drops for an evening. Fees start from USD 423/month for Primary and vary by curriculum and level."
