        "h": "Subjects that are hard to staff outside the capital",
        "p": "The gap outside Nairobi is mostly specialist teaching. A Level Further Mathematics, Physics, Chemistry, Computer Science and Economics need teachers who are scarce in any town, and a school with three interested students cannot justify one. A live group drawn from Mombasa, Kisumu, Eldoret and abroad can. Because Kenya and our teachers are on the same clock, lessons sit in the normal school day or straight after it, and every one is recorded. Families who visit Nairobi can also use our Parklands centre. Fees start from USD 423/month for Primary (about KSh 54,600 at the October 2026 rate) and vary by curriculum and level. The class is small enough for every student to speak, and the teacher marks every piece of work."
