    "intro": "Most writing about international schooling in the DRC is about two places: Kinshasa, which has the American school, the French lycée and the Belgian school, and the cobalt belt around Kolwezi, which has the mining companies and almost no schools to match. We have written about both. This guide is about the rest of a very large country, where most Congolese families live: Kisangani on the river, Goma and Bukavu in the Kivus, Mbuji-Mayi and Kananga in the Kasaï, and Matadi on the way to the sea. It looks at the clock, the language and the final years of secondary school.",
