        "p": "Kisangani is the great river city of the north-east. Goma and Bukavu, on the shores of Lake Kivu, have long hosted one of the largest humanitarian and UN presences in Africa, alongside traders and families with links across the borders with Rwanda, Uganda and Burundi. Mbuji-Mayi is the diamond city of the Kasaï. Matadi is the country’s main seaport, on the road from Kinshasa to the Atlantic. Each has Congolese schools, many of them run by the churches and well regarded. Almost none offers an English-medium international curriculum, and in the east, conditions can change quickly, which makes a school that does not depend on a building more useful than it sounds. For families in these cities the traditional answer has been boarding in Kinshasa, in a neighbouring country or in Belgium."
