        "p": "The loi-cadre of 2014 guarantees notable parental liberties, including the freedom of parents to choose the type of education corresponding to their convictions. That is not a home-education right, and private establishments in the DRC require agrément. Smartious is not an agréé Congolese establishment, so we work alongside a Congolese school, which continues its own national track unchanged. A proposal to modify the loi-cadre was tabled in April 2026; it is pending, not law. A family whose plans depend on the legal position should confirm it with the ministry responsible for national education. We say this at admissions because a careless reading of the liberties clause could mislead a family."
