        "p": "Most stay with the local school and the NSC, which is a sound qualification and the right one for a child heading to a South African university. Some board, often far from home, in the independent schools of the Midlands, the Eastern Cape or the metros. And a large and growing number home-educate, registered with their provincial education department and often using established CAPS-aligned online or correspondence providers. All three are reasonable. The gap they leave is narrow: live, specialist teaching toward Cambridge or Pearson Edexcel examinations for families outside the metros, and a qualification that does not need translating for families whose next home may be in Manchester, Perth or Toronto."
