        "p": "The subjects families ask for are specific. Physics and Chemistry as separate A-Levels, where the NSC combines them as Physical Sciences. Further Mathematics, which suits students heading for engineering or actuarial science abroad. Computer Science and Economics where a school cannot staff a small set. American-curriculum AP courses and IB subject support for US- or IB-bound students. Fees start from USD 423 a month for Primary, about R 7,700 at a rate of around 18 rand to the dollar, and vary by curriculum and level. But a child settled at a good school, doing well in the NSC and aiming at UCT, Wits or Stellenbosch, does not need us, and I would rather say that plainly than sell around it."
