        "p": "Our other Botswana guide covers the diamond towns, Francistown and the Delta. These families are further still from a campus. Ghanzi and the western Kalahari run on cattle ranching and the new copper mines of the Kalahari Copperbelt. Tsabong and the Kgalagadi villages are among the most remote communities in the country. Serowe and Palapye, home to BIUST and the Morupule power station, sit in the Central District, and the Tuli Block’s farms lie along the eastern border. For senior students in all of these places, boarding in Gaborone or South Africa has been the usual answer. Live teaching, alongside the local senior school, lets a student stay home through Form 5 and beyond."
