        "p": "Sur, around 150 kilometres from Muscat, hosts Oman LNG. Sohar, on the Batinah coast to the north, has its port, free zone and heavy industry. Duqm, on the central Arabian Sea coast, has grown around its special economic zone, port and refinery. Each brings engineers and technical families on contracts of a few years, often with children at the end of primary or in secondary school. Local schools serve these towns, but the subject list at upper secondary is narrow. The arrangement that works is two or three subjects with us alongside the local school, or, for an expatriate family who has confirmed its own position, a full programme. Either way the curriculum continues unchanged when the contract moves on."
