        "p": "By the last two school years, the university target should decide the subjects. In Oman that may be Sultan Qaboos University, the German University of Technology in Oman or the University of Nizwa; abroad, UCAS, the Common Application or a university elsewhere in the Gulf. Oman’s Ministry of Education issues equivalency for foreign qualifications, and each university sets its own requirements, so ask both before subjects are fixed, and ask whether private-candidate results are accepted. Cambridge and Pearson Edexcel exams are taken as a private candidate through British Council Oman in Muscat, with entry deadlines months before each series. Choosing well in Year 12 avoids a scramble in Year 13."
