        "h": "The rules, and when the local school is right",
        "p": "Oman’s Ministry of Education regulates schools. Omani law does not set out a specific process for homeschooling. Expatriate families commonly use international online schools, especially for IGCSE and A Level. Rules can differ for Omani citizens and for residents, so check your situation with the Ministry, and ask about equivalency and transfer requirements before you start. Smartious claims no approval from the Ministry. And the local school is often the right answer: if your child is settled and the subjects they need are taught, keep it. If your child may later join an Omani school, keep every report and certificate, because the school and the Ministry will ask for them. The cases where we help most are specific: a missing subject, a thin A Level set, or a town too far from the capital for a daily drive."
