    "intro": "France has a large international-school sector, and most of it sits around Paris, in the western suburbs where multinational and diplomatic families live. The international economy is far more spread out than that. Airbus builds aircraft in Toulouse, Sanofi and bioMérieux anchor Lyon’s life-sciences cluster, Sophia Antipolis hosts one of Europe’s largest technology parks, and Strasbourg is home to the European Parliament and the Council of Europe. This guide is about families in those places, and about the role a live online school can honestly play in a country whose home-education law is clear and deliberately strict.",
