    "intro": "The Netherlands is one of the easiest countries in Europe to explain, because the law leaves little room for interpretation. Children are leerplichtig from five through the school year in which they turn sixteen, the duty is met by enrolment at a recognised school, and an unrecognised online school does not satisfy it. So I will say at the start what we are here: a supplementary school, working alongside a Dutch or international enrolment. Within that, there is a great deal of useful work to do, and this guide explains where it is.",
