        "p": "Eindhoven’s engineering families ask for Mathematics, Further Mathematics, Physics and Computer Science, often for children who may apply to UK universities. The Hague’s institutional families want continuity: an English-medium record in English, History and the sciences that survives a move to Geneva, New York or Nairobi. Rotterdam’s shipping and trading families ask for Economics and Business beside Mathematics. Families on a Cambridge track at an IB school use us for the IGCSE or A-Level subject the school does not offer. A student in a Dutch havo or vwo stream who wants an English-taught degree abroad uses A-Levels to strengthen the application. These are subjects a busy Dutch timetable cannot add for one or two students."
