        "h": "The legal edges, and when the local school is enough",
        "p": "There is one narrow exemption in Dutch law, Article 5 under b of the Leerplichtwet, for parents with overriding objections to the religious or philosophical direction of every school within reasonable distance. The Hoge Raad tightened it in April 2026, enforcement is resuming, and it is essentially unavailable once a child has been enrolled at a school of that direction. We do not advise on it; families considering it need a Dutch education lawyer. For families who already lawfully hold that exemption, we provide structured curriculum without claims attached. And for a child thriving in a Dutch school with a Dutch university in mind, the school is the right answer on its own."
