    "intro": "Japan’s international families are concentrated and easy to describe. They are in Tokyo, especially Minato and Setagaya; in Yokohama; in Kansai between Osaka and Kobe; around Nagoya and the Toyota supply chain; and in Okinawa, around the US bases. Alongside them is a group that is particular to Japan: kikokushijo, Japanese children returning from years abroad, often fluent in English and educated in Cambridge, IB or American schools. The international schools that serve these families, the American School in Japan, the British School in Tokyo, Yokohama International School, Canadian Academy in Kobe and others, are excellent and full-time. This guide is about the families for whom a full-time international school is not the answer, and what a live online school can do after the Japanese school day ends.",
