        "p": "Most choose two or three subjects: English Language or Literature to keep academic English strong, Mathematics, and one or two of Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Economics or Computer Science. These lead to Cambridge IGCSE and A-Level, or Pearson Edexcel equivalents, and AP for families with US plans. Cambridge and Pearson Edexcel examinations are sat at authorised exam centres, which families book; most are in Tokyo, and centres are confirmed per family, per session. Students who start at twelve or thirteen typically sit IGCSE at fifteen or sixteen, and can then continue to A-Level while finishing Japanese high school. AP suits students bound for US universities who want college-level courses on their record. For families outside Tokyo, exam travel is a few trips a year by Shinkansen or plane."
