        "h": "Honest limits",
        "p": "A Japanese school day, followed by club activities and then an online class, is a long day, and we would rather a child take two subjects well than four badly. We do not replace the campus, sport and community of an international school, and for families who want and can access that, it is the better choice. And a child fully settled in Japanese school and aiming at a Japanese university through the Common Test does not need us; the Japanese system serves that goal well. We also say plainly that a returnee child’s Japanese matters; keeping the Japanese school strong is part of the plan, not an obstacle to it. We will tell you if we think the load is too heavy."
