    "intro": "Taiwan has some of the most respected international schools in Asia, and most Taiwanese children cannot attend them. That is not a matter of fees or waiting lists. Taiwan’s international schools are, in general, not permitted to enrol children who hold only Taiwanese citizenship. So the market splits in two. On one side are foreign and dual-passport families, well served in Taipei and reasonably served in Hsinchu, Taichung and Kaohsiung. On the other are Taiwanese families who want an English-medium, internationally examined route for their children and have, until recently, had to assemble it from bilingual schools, cram classes and private tutors. This guide is about where a live online school fits for both groups, and where it does not.",
