    "intro": "Indonesia stretches across three time zones and thousands of inhabited islands, and its international schooling is concentrated in a handful of places. Jakarta has the largest tier by far, with Bali, Surabaya, Bandung and Batam following. The international economy is much wider than that. It runs through the coal and energy towns of Kalimantan, the nickel smelters of Sulawesi, the mines of Papua, the shipyards facing Singapore and the resorts of Bali and Lombok. This guide is about the families that economy brings in or creates, Indonesian and expatriate, what they do for school now, and where a live online school honestly fits. Our separate guide on homeschooling law covers sekolahrumah and the Paket exams in detail.",
