        "p": "Families in the energy, mining and shipbuilding towns tend to ask for Mathematics, Physics and Chemistry, the subjects behind engineering degrees. Jakarta’s corporate families add Economics and Business. Families aiming at US universities take the American curriculum with AP; those aiming at Canada can take the Ontario Secondary School Diploma through our Ontario partner school. Cambridge and Pearson Edexcel examinations are sat at authorised centres, including the British Council in Jakarta, which families book. The limits are real. We cannot give a child a campus, school sport or daily friendships, and we do not teach the national curriculum’s Indonesian language, Pancasila and civics, or religion. A student settled at a good SPK school or national school, heading for an Indonesian university, may well not need us."
