    "conclusion": "Indonesia’s international economy reaches from Batam to Papua, and its international schools reach a few cities. A live Cambridge, Pearson, IB or American programme taught in the Indonesian afternoon, from USD 423/month for Primary and varying by curriculum and level, reaches every island the same way, alongside a school or as the core of a homeschool. If that fits your family, book an assessment for your child."
